    <note id="bVk">
      <content>
        <p>This table shows why we do not see a direct competitor. Chat-to-code tools generate code, but they have no checkable world, no continuous society, and no market. Video world models produce impressive clips, but they are not truly playable or auditable. The NPC-town research pioneered living agents, but those demos are not playable, not checkable, and not monetized. OpenGame is the only system that combines all five: a playable surface, a checkable world, continuous living evolution, opinion and rumor dynamics, and a prediction market on top. The moat is not any single feature; it is the combination, because each layer makes the others more valuable. A competitor would have to build all five at once, and they are already integrated and running.</p>
      </content>
    </note>
